<item>
            <title>[LU-20581] sanity-lnet test_50 allocates the default 1 GiB router pool</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20581</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;test_50 enables routing through a yaml import without setting any router buffer parameter, so LNet allocates its default pool. On a node with limited memory the import fails:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;/usr/sbin/lnetctl import /tmp/sanity-lnet-50.yaml
---
add:
-     import:
      errno: -12
      descr: ! &quot;Out of memory&quot;
...
 sanity-lnet test_50: @@@@@@ FAIL: Import failed rc = 234
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The kernel reports the size of the request:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;LNetError: lnet_rtrpool_adjust_bufs()) lnet: error allocating 1024x256 page router buffers on CPT 0: rc = -12
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That is LNET_NRB_LARGE (1024) buffers of LNET_MTU (1 MiB) each, so about 1 GiB, plus LNET_NRB_SMALL 4 KiB buffers for another 64 MiB. lnet_nrb_*_calculate() divides the count by LNET_CPT_NUMBER and lnet_rtrpools_alloc() then allocates that many per CPT, so the total is about 1.06 GiB whatever the CPU count.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The test passes in isolation on a 1385 MB node and fails when run after the preceding subtests, once the page cache is populated.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Other tests that enable routing do not hit this because setup_router_test() sets the counts as lnet module parameters:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;	mod_opts+=&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot; large_router_buffers=4&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
	mod_opts+=&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot; small_router_buffers=8&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
	mod_opts+=&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot; tiny_router_buffers=$NTRB&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_50 should do the same. tiny_router_buffers, small_router_buffers and large_router_buffers are all module_param(..., 0444), so they can only be set when lnet is loaded; the test currently calls reinit_dlc(), which reuses an already configured LNet.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
